  "worked_solution": "We model the number of subscribers using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.01S.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.01t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the service currently has $10\\,000$ subscribers, so we have ${S}_{0}=10\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the number of subscribers $S$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nS(t)=10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.01t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of subscribers when $t=10,$ we substitute $t=10$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(10) & =10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.01\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =10\\,000\\,{e}^{0.1} \\\\  & \u224811\\,051.71\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that the number of subscribers is $11\\,052$ after $10$ weeks.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
